    {
      "description": "DATEDIFF semantics on lines 141 and 142, with AsOfDate 2025-12-31 (a Wednesday). Every claim has a non-zero day gap, so a Spark datediff(start, end) with the arguments reversed would give negative days_since_activity and push claims into the wrong band. DATEDIFF(WEEK) counts the Sundays crossed, which differs from floor(days/7) in these claims: claim 1 reported 2025-12-26 (Friday, 5 days, crosses 12-28); claim 2 reported 2025-12-20 (Saturday, 11 days, crosses 12-21 and 12-28); claim 3 reported 2025-12-27 (Saturday, 4 days). Claim 4 is reported on a Sunday, 2025-12-21, and is a control case where both methods agree. Claim 5 (reported 2025-09-06, a Saturday, with payments) and claim 6 (reported 2025-11-29, a Saturday, unpaid) cover longer gaps. Some payments fall after the reporting date and must be ignored.",
